## FOLDER STRUCTURE RULES

### 1. Feature-based organization  
- Every feature must have its own folder under `tests/e2e/` or `tests/api/` or other test type folders.
- A feature must always include the following:
  - `cases/` folder containing test cases
  - `shared-data.json` file for feature-level shared data
- Each case folder contains its own `results/` folder for test execution results

### 2. Test Case Organization  
- Each test case must be organized in its own folder under `cases/`.
- Test case folder naming: `<descriptive-case-name>/` (e.g., `login-successful/`, `add-product-to-cart/`)
- Each case folder must contain:
  - `test.spec.ts` - Main test script (required)
  - `test-data.json` - Test data specific to this case (required)
  - `scenario.md` - Scenario documentation with test steps and expected results (required)
  - `results/` - Test execution results folder (auto-created when tests run)
  - Optional files:
    - `assertions.ts` - Assertion functions (if assertions are complex)
    - `constants.ts` - Case-specific constants (if needed)

### 3. Test Script Files  
- All test scripts must be named `test.spec.ts` and placed in:
```
tests/e2e/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/test.spec.ts
tests/api/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/test.spec.ts
tests/performance/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/test.spec.ts
tests/regression/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/test.spec.ts
tests/security/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/test.spec.ts
tests/ui/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/test.spec.ts
```

### 4. Scenario Documentation  
- Scenario documentation is required and must be stored as:
```
tests/e2e/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/scenario.md
```
- Must include:
  - Test Case ID and metadata
  - Test scenario description
  - Detailed test steps
  - Expected results
  - Test data reference
- Same pattern applies to all test types (api, performance, regression, security, ui)

### 5. Test Data Files  
- Test data must be stored in:
```
tests/e2e/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/test-data.json
```
- Feature-level shared data must be stored in:
```
tests/e2e/<feature-name>/shared-data.json
```
- Same pattern applies to all test types (api, performance, regression, security, ui)

### 6. Page Object Model  
- All POM classes must be placed in:
```
src/pages/<page-name>-page.ts
```
- Example: `src/pages/login-page.ts`, `src/pages/dashboard-page.ts`

### 7. Utilities & Helpers  
- All reusable utilities belong under:
```
src/utils/<utility-name>.ts
```
- Example: `src/utils/file-utils.ts`, `src/utils/test-output-helper.ts`

### 8. Fixtures  
- All Playwright fixtures must be placed here:
```
src/fixtures/<fixture-name>.fixture.ts
```
- Example: `src/fixtures/auth.fixture.ts`, `src/fixtures/data.fixture.ts`

### 9. Constants & Configuration  
- Environment constants: `src/constants/env.ts`
- Selectors: `src/constants/selectors.ts`
- Test data constants: `src/constants/test-data.ts`

### 10. API Clients  
- All API client classes must be placed in:
```
src/api/<api-client-name>.ts
```
- Example: `src/api/user-api.ts`, `src/api/product-api.ts`

### 11. Mocks  
- All mock data and mock servers must be placed in:
```
src/mocks/<mock-name>.ts
```
- Example: `src/mocks/user-mock.ts`, `src/mocks/api-responses.json`

### 12. Test Reports  
- Must be output to:
```
reports/
```
- Allure reports: `reports/allure/`
- Should not be committed to git.

### 13. Test Results (Screenshots, Videos, Logs)  
- Test execution results are stored in:
```
tests/e2e/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/results/
tests/api/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/results/
tests/performance/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/results/
tests/regression/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/results/
tests/security/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/results/
tests/ui/<feature-name>/cases/<case-folder-name>/results/
```
- Each test execution creates files and folders inside the case's `results/` folder containing:
  - `screenshots/` - Screenshot files
  - `logs/` - Page source, test result JSON files
  - `videos/` - Video recordings (if enabled)
  - `traces/` - Trace files (if enabled)
- Results are organized per case, making it easier to find test artifacts for specific test cases
- Global test results may also be stored in `allure-results/` folder at root level

### 14. Global Setup / Teardown  
- Must be placed at the root of the tests folder:
- `tests/global-setup.ts`
- `tests/global-teardown.ts`

